---
// A store discount link, /discount/<code>/ (cmh-golang's shop module builds them; the apps open
// them). public/_redirects REWRITES every /discount/* path to this one static page (a 200, so the
// address keeps the code), and the script below forwards to /shop/?discount=<code>, where the cart
// client keeps the code for the cart. Pages cannot put a path placeholder into a redirect's query
// string (it sends ":code" literally), which is why this is a page and not a redirect.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>SeeMyHealth</title>
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var match = window.location.pathname.match(/^\/discount\/([A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64})\/?$/);
        var target = match ? "/shop/?discount=" + encodeURIComponent(match[1]) : "/shop/";
        window.location.replace(target);
      })();
    </script>
    <noscript><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/shop/" /></noscript>
  </head>
  <body></body>
</html>
